---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const objects = [
	['WORKPLACE', 'Declared durable boundary and shared constitution.'],
	['MEMBER', 'A durable human identity in the Workplace.'],
	['DESK', 'Optional local continuity and Route ownership for one Member.'],
	['ROOM', 'A durable domain with its own mission and Material.'],
	['EQUIPMENT', 'A reusable way of working and its projections.'],
	['SITE', 'A sovereign external authority, usually a Git repository.'],
	['ROUTE', 'A Desk-owned relationship to one Site.'],
	['CHECKOUT', 'The derived local address of a Route, never its owner.'],
	['MEETING', 'The current ephemeral work event.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Homes in practice | Endroit"
	description="How the Endroit 0.10 Profile composes owned Documents, Material, Equipment, Sites and Routes into a durable human-agent Workplace."
	path="/homes/"
	current="homes"
>
	<main id="main" class="page-instrument">
		<section class="module page-hero" aria-labelledby="homes-title">
			<div>
				<p class="module-plate">FIELD GUIDE · HOME / 01</p>
				<h1 id="homes-title">Start with the place that survives the session.</h1>
				<p class="page-lede">A Workplace is not a giant prompt or a persistent agent. It is a declared durable boundary whose owned meaning remains legible when the executor changes.</p>
				<div class="hero-actions">
					<a class="action action-primary" href="/install/">Create a Workplace</a>
					<a class="action" href="/profile.md">Read the Profile source</a>
					<a class="action" href="https://github.com/thevzion/endroit">Inspect the source</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="screen page-screen">
				<div class="screen-face home-map" aria-hidden="true">
					<span>WORKPLACE</span><i></i><span>ROOM</span><i></i><span>MEETING</span>
					<b>owns</b><b>locates</b><b>expires</b>
				</div>
				<figcaption>Durable place on the left. Ephemeral work on the right. Ownership stays visible all the way through.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</section>

		<section class="module" aria-labelledby="bootstrap-title">
			<p class="module-plate">MODULE · MINIMUM VIABLE PLACE</p>
			<h2 id="bootstrap-title">A Member, a Desk and one Room are enough to begin.</h2>
			<div class="page-two-up">
			<pre class="source-tree"><code>my-workplace/
├── WORKPLACE.md
├── members/me/MEMBER.md
├── rooms/home/ROOM.md
└── .desk/
	    └── DESK.md</code></pre>
				<div class="module-copy">
					<p><code>endroit create</code> keeps the initial Desk in the Workplace Git by default. <code>endroit init</code> uses a separate nested Desk repository by default. <code>--desk tracked|separate|later</code> makes that boundary explicit.</p>
					<p>Provider front doors are generated from owned sources. More Rooms, Sites and Equipment appear only when real work needs them.</p>
					<p class="module-note">The <code>0.10.0-alpha.0</code> candidate writes native v9 Workplace, Member, Desk and Route Documents. Room, Site and most Equipment and Artifact writers remain on their documented compatibility surfaces.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="module" aria-labelledby="objects-title">
			<p class="module-plate">MODULE · ENDROIT PROFILE</p>
			<h2 id="objects-title">One concrete vocabulary for shared responsibilities.</h2>
			<div class="signal-table object-table">
				{objects.map(([name, copy], index) => (
					<div class="signal-row"><span class="signal-index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{name}</strong><span>{copy}</span></div>
				))}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="module" aria-labelledby="composition-title">
			<p class="module-plate">MODULE · COMPOSITION</p>
			<h2 id="composition-title">Methods equip a place. They do not own it.</h2>
			<div class="bench-cards">
				<article><p class="card-signal">ROOM</p><h3>Start from the domain</h3><p>Give one coherent subject a mission, Material and continuity before choosing a runtime or method.</p></article>
				<article><p class="card-signal">EQUIPMENT</p><h3>Add a way of working</h3><p>Research, planning or publishing can be installed and removed without absorbing the Room.</p></article>
				<article><p class="card-signal">MEETING</p><h3>Execute for now</h3><p>The work event is ephemeral. Retention, acceptance and external effects remain distinct explicit transitions.</p></article>
				<article><p class="card-signal signal-live">SITE + ROUTE</p><h3>Relate without absorption</h3><p>A Site keeps its authority while a Desk declares a Route and Endroit derives a local Checkout address.</p></article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="module page-terminal" aria-labelledby="home-question">
			<p class="module-plate">TRIGGER · START WITH THE PLACE</p>
			<h2 id="home-question">What should still make sense when the agent changes?</h2>
			<p class="module-lede">That is the first question a Workplace answers.</p>
			<a class="action action-primary" href="/install/">Install Endroit</a>
		</section>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>
